.TH "PKGCATALOG\-SCAN" "1" "" "libpkgcatalog\-acquire 3.0.0" "libpkgcatalog\-acquire"
.SH NAME
pkgcatalog\-scan \- validate and inspect explicit native package collections
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
pkgcatalog\-scan [\-\-max\-document\-bytes N]
  \-\-collection NAME=ROOT [\-\-collection NAME=ROOT ...]
  [\-\-external\-revision NAME=REVISION ...]
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[CR]pkgcatalog\-scan\f[R] is the reference client for \f[CR]libpkgcatalog\-acquire\f[R].
Repeated \f[CR]\-\-collection\f[R] arguments receive contiguous precedence in command\-line order.
The command acquires the native layout and prints the catalog identity, collection revision identities, and effective and shadowed candidates.
.PP
The output is diagnostic text.
It is not a durable catalog record, resolver protocol, or package\-manager configuration format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-collection NAME=ROOT\f[R]
Add one explicit collection.
Repetition order defines precedence from zero.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-external\-revision NAME=REVISION\f[R]
Attach diagnostic revision provenance to one configured collection.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-max\-document\-bytes N\f[R]
Set a positive canonical decimal byte ceiling for each YAML document.
The default is 1048576.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-version\f[R]
Print the program version.
.TP
\f[CR]\-\-help\f[R]
Print usage.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates a successfully sealed catalog.
Non\-zero indicates option, filesystem, YAML, source\-authority, or catalog\-authority failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]pkgcatalog_acquire(3)\f[R], \f[CR]pkgcatalog_collection_layout(5)\f[R], \f[CR]libpkgcatalog(3)\f[R]
